<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Isandlwana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1879">1879</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-zulu-war">Anglo-Zulu War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Isandlwana was fought on 22 January 1879, at the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-zulu-war">Anglo-Zulu War</a>, when some 20,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> warriors overran the camp of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederic-thesiger-2nd-baron-chelmsford">Lord Chelmsford</a>'s centre column below Isandlwana hill. More than 1,300 British soldiers and African auxiliaries were killed. It was one of the worst defeats suffered by a British army against an indigenous force and caused a political shock in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-isandlwana.jpg" alt="Battle of Isandlwana" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Edwin Fripp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Isandhlwana.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
